{"t": 1794110418.1097453, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f Production regression from this change (commit 8c2f1d0).\n\nSentry issue **LEDGER-WORKER-9A** \u2014 `ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099)`:\nhttps://acme.sentry.io/issues/?query=LEDGER-WORKER-9A\n\nReplacing `round(amount_minor * rate)` with `int(amount_minor * rate)` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so any conversion with a fractional part >= 0.5 loses one minor unit (e.g. `99999 * 0.011 = 1099.989` -> `1099` instead of `1100`). First seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`, 2,201 events so far.\n\nFix: restored `round(amount_minor * rate)` in `worker/rates.py`. Please be careful with the \"speed up\" optimization here \u2014 correctness of minor-unit rounding matters more than the micro-optimization.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
